  <text>
    <body>
      <div>
        <head>In the directories</head>
        <p>R. or Robt. W. Hewat, hairdresser, is listed in <ref target="civic?id=Bouverie%20Street">Bouverie Street</ref> from 1915 to 1940. He is at No. 193, next to the fire station, in 1915 and 1920, and at No. 166, on the <ref target="civic?id=Church%20Street">Church Street</ref> corner, from 1925. No trade is given in 1940.</p>
        <p>A Robert Hewat is listed at No. 93 <ref target="civic?id=Madeline%20Street">Madeline Street</ref> in 1910. That listing is not linked to this entry.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <head>On the electoral roll</head>
        <p>Robert William Hewat, hairdresser, is on the 1928 <ref target="civic?id=Electoral-Rolls">electoral roll</ref> at 166 Bouverie Street, with Rose Hewat, home duties.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <head>Neighbours</head>
        <p>After he moved, No. 193 was taken by <ref target="civic?id=Alexander%20James%20Barbour">Alexander James Barbour</ref>, stone mason. At No. 166 his neighbours at No. 168 are Wm. Wing (1925), Mrs Ellen Davis (1930), Mrs Florence E. Yates (1935) and Mrs Alice Bennett (1940).</p>
      </div>
